# Build context for the service images (services/*/Dockerfile), which are built from the
# repository root. Docker applies the LAST pattern that matches a path (or one of its parent
# directories), so the order below matters. tests/tooling/test_container_images.py checks this
# file, including that section 2 lists exactly what the images install.

# 1. Nothing by default: .git, .worktrees, .venv, web/, infra/ (Terraform state, plans,
#    .terraform, tfvars), scripts/, docs/, the root files, tests and examples stay out.
*

# 2. Allow-list: exactly what `pip install` needs to build each library and service, which is
#    its pyproject.toml, its README.md (the `readme` of the package metadata) and the package
#    directories its pyproject.toml names. A new library or service adds its own lines here.
!libs/pulsebridge_fhir/pyproject.toml
!libs/pulsebridge_fhir/README.md
!libs/pulsebridge_fhir/pulsebridge_fhir/
!libs/pulsebridge_gcp/pyproject.toml
!libs/pulsebridge_gcp/README.md
!libs/pulsebridge_gcp/pulsebridge_gcp/
!libs/pulsebridge_hl7v2/pyproject.toml
!libs/pulsebridge_hl7v2/README.md
!libs/pulsebridge_hl7v2/pulsebridge_hl7v2/
!libs/pulsebridge_hl7v2/samples/
!services/cuff-sim/pyproject.toml
!services/cuff-sim/README.md
!services/cuff-sim/cuff_sim/
!services/health-sync/pyproject.toml
!services/health-sync/README.md
!services/health-sync/health_sync/
!services/v2-to-fhir/pyproject.toml
!services/v2-to-fhir/README.md
!services/v2-to-fhir/v2_to_fhir/

# 3. Deny-list, the second line of defence: never sent even from inside an allowed directory.
# Secrets and key files (a service account key under its console name is
# <project>-<12 hex>.json).
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.envrc
**/.netrc
**/.pypirc
**/id_rsa*
**/id_dsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets
**/token*.json
**/*credentials*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/*sa-key*.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
# Terraform state, plans and variables.
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json
**/*.tfplan
# Local environments, caches, build output and tests.
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/dist
**/tests
**/Dockerfile
